# WildfireGuardian Route-Check API: runtime settings (all optional).
# The API uses no API keys, tokens or other secrets, and makes no network calls at runtime.
# Copy this file to api/.env (git-ignored) and load it into your shell (shell syntax) before `make api`:
#   set -a; . api/.env; set +a
# Experiment constants (30 s budget, 3072 MiB guard, 300 m snap, 10 kW/m2, 100 kJ/m2, 120 s) are fixed in api/config.py.

# Root of the recorded inputs (graphs/, latest_inputs_try02/). Default: <repo>/data/routing
# WFG_API_DATA_ROOT=data/routing

# Job folders, the ablation kit copy and per-request packets. Default: <repo>/artifacts/api_runtime (git-ignored)
# WFG_API_RUNTIME_DIR=artifacts/api_runtime

# Concurrent route checks (spawn process pool). Default: physical cores - 2 (minimum 1)
# WFG_API_WORKERS=4

# Bind address and port. Defaults: 127.0.0.1 and 8765
# WFG_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# WFG_API_PORT=8765

# Interpreter that launches kit workers and child processes. Default: the server's sys.executable
# WFG_API_PYTHON=.venv/bin/python

# Fallback git commit for provenance, used only when the repository root is not the top of its own git work tree.
# WFG_API_GIT_COMMIT=

# Step 9 live road state from crossing units (WS /v1/live/closures). Off unless exactly 1. With it off, nothing changes.
# WFG_API_LIVE_CLOSURES=1
# Optional shared token for WS /v1/live/closures, sent by the crossing client in Sec-WebSocket-Protocol
# ("wfg-live.v1, wfg-token.<token>"; letters, digits, "-" and "_" only). Set it, the socket refuses connections without it.
# WFG_API_LIVE_TOKEN=
# Exact browser Origins allowed to open the live socket (comma separated). Default: none (the Python client sends no Origin).
# WFG_API_LIVE_ORIGINS=
# Extra Host names allowed on the live socket besides 127.0.0.1, localhost, [::1] and WFG_API_HOST (DNS-rebinding guard).
# WFG_API_LIVE_HOSTS=
